-- title:
--   Two minimal primes over varpi in the j-chart of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M\ge 5$, nonzero, with $p\nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A\to L\to K$. Let $j\in K$ be an element whose image in $L((q))$ is the coefficientwise image of the rational $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant, assumed nonzero, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Write $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ (resp. $A_{\mathrm{inf}}$) for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$ (resp. over $A[j^{-1}]$), these being `chartAlgFin` and `chartAlgInf`. Then the ideal of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ generated by the image of $\varpi$ has exactly two minimal primes, and for every minimal prime $Q$ of the ideal of $A_{\mathrm{inf}}$ generated by the image of $\varpi$ one has $j^{-1}\notin Q$.
--
--   This is the arithmetic of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring containing $\zeta_p$: the fibre over the uniformiser has exactly two vertical branches in the $j$-finite chart, and in the chart at $j=\infty$ no branch passes through the locus $j^{-1}=0$, in accordance with the Deligne–Rapoport description of the reduction of $X_1(Mp)$ in characteristic $p$. It is used in the statements producing the two irreducible components of the pullback of the model to the residue characteristic.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_ncard_minimalPrimes_span_chartAlgFin_eq_two_and_jInvChartInf_notMem_x1_mul.lean

